OL,3,GNEWSAMayor backs #1bn battery-electric
OL,4,Atrain project
OL,5,
OL,6,FLocal politicians have welcomed a #1bn
OL,7,Fproject to build the UK's first
OL,8,Fbattery-electric train fleet for long
OL,9,Fdistance mainline services.
OL,11,FThe Department for Transport (DfT)
OL,12,Fannounced plans to upgrade TransPennine
OL,13,Ftrains that run between northern
OL,14,Fcities, including Hull. They will be
OL,15,Fpowered by overhead electric wires and
OL,16,Fbatteries.
OL,18,FHull was not included in the #45bn
OL,19,FNorthern Powerhouse Rail (NPR) scheme
OL,20,Fannounced in January, which will see
OL,21,Flines electrified between Leeds, York
OL,22,Fand Sheffield.
OL,23,APub: 14-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
